## Review: M4 trellis-GEMM default + profiling timer fix

No blocking correctness issues found. Ranked findings:

**1. Planned final body — verified, no issue.**
`raw.map_or_else(|| crate::utils::is_base_m4(brand), |value| value == "1")` satisfies all 10 cases in `trellis_gemm_default_is_m4_only_and_preserves_explicit_overrides` (eschamoe.rs:1802), including the `" Apple M4 "` trim and `Some("0")`/`Some("yes")` overrides. Caveats, not bugs: exact `"Apple M4"` match excludes Pro/Max/M5 (deliberate) and any future variant spelling; brand detection failing (bare `"sysctl"` PATH lookup at utils.rs:1173 vs absolute `/usr/sbin/sysctl` at state.rs:2250) silently degrades to default-off — execution and identity stay consistent since both share the cached source, so this is a silent-policy, not a fingerprint, risk.

**2. Fingerprint agreement — holds.**
Execution `trellis_gemm_mode()` (eschamoe.rs:1404), engine identity (runtime_identity.rs:177), and capacity logging (state.rs:2071) all route through `resolve_trellis_gemm_mode` / shared cached `apple_cpu_brand`. Only divergence path: env mutated after the OnceLock pins — `set_var` exists only in ignored/manual tests and doctor-restore, not production. Low.

**3. Doc drift on flip (must fix when landing the final body).**
eschamoe.rs:1397 "The default is the scratch path" and :1401-1402 "SIMD selection only applies after GEMM is explicitly enabled" become false on base M4; docs/models.md:201 likewise. Flipping also changes `eschamoeTrellisGemm` in the runtime identity on M4 → identity-keyed persisted state gets a new key once (intended; rollout-visible).

**4. Profiling timers — semantics changed, consumers must know.**
- `PROF_TQ_ATTN_NS` no longer includes projections + cache append (timer now starts after append eval, qwen3_next.rs:4683-4709); previously collected attn_ms is not comparable to new runs.
- Q-projection time is now invisible in both buckets (Q eval moved before both timers, :4677).
- canonical branch unaffected: `tq_prof` requires L==1, `canonical_rows` requires L>1 — mutually exclusive, so the old early timer was dead there too.
- `let _ =` → `?` on evals: under profiling, eval failure now aborts the forward instead of skipping timing. Arguably correct; flag-only behavior change.
- `profiling` ungated from `T == 1` (:8796): prefill now gets per-layer barriers on the sampled prefix. "bounded prefill chunks" (:8792) is enforced by the serving stack's chunking, not here — an unchunked large-T forward barrier-syncs per sampled layer. Diagnostic-only; `query_tokens = T` (:8934) makes extrapolation misuse detectable. Acceptable.

**5. Accidental production changes — none found.**
All attention-path edits are `tq_prof`-gated; today's `trellis_gemm_mode_for_brand` body is exactly equivalent to the old check (incl. non-UTF-8 env → false); `is_base_m4` is logic-identical to the old inline match; the engine identity field resolves identically under the current body.

**6. Test fragility (low).**
`escha_identity_describes_the_executing_kernel_default` (runtime_identity.rs:273) compares live-env identity against OnceLock-cached `trellis_gemm_mode()` — policy-agnostic and stays green through the flip, but is order-sensitive if anything in the higgs-engine unit-test binary ever mutates `HIGGS_ESCHA_TRELLIS_GEMM` (nothing currently does; the dflash env harness is ignored/manual, the integration test is a separate binary). The eschamoe RED test is pure (no env/brand dependence) — correctly pins the planned policy.

Per instructions, no performance claims are made from source; the pending seven matched-behavior cases and AC measurements are outside this diff.
